      "artist": "whatsthatpicture from Hanwell, London, UK",
      "description": "If my memory serves me correctly, and EastMarple1 will probably jump straight in and confirm or correct this, this is highly likely to be where the Hook family lived at 192 Springfield Road, Chelmsford.  It doesn't look like this address exists any more, and is right by the site of Chelmsford Prison.\nThe house, and especially that back door, appears in many shots in the album.  As does the driveway.\nI shall have to see if I can consult some contemporary maps to see if the layout matches.\nNot often you get vernacular images from such an early date.\n\n\nSee more images from this fascinating Edwardian Hook family album.",
